content.text:
Fixed. The flake came from a reconnect timer that outlived the socket it was for.

- `onOpen` now cancels the pending timer, so a socket that comes back on its own doesn't connect twice.
- `scheduleReconnect` clears any earlier timer before arming a new one.
- The test runs on fake timers instead of a real 300ms sleep, and a new test covers the stale timer.

The core of the change:

```ts
export function onOpen(socket: RelaySocket) {
  clearTimeout(socket.timer);
  socket.timer = undefined;
  socket.attempt = 0;
}
```

`bun test reconnect --rerun-each 50` passes 100 of 100.
